---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
EVM chains: read-only contract calls, decoding, logs, transactions, blocks, ENS and local Anvil forks

Usage: rustman evm [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  call    Run a read-only contract call (an evm-call request file, or --to, --abi and --function) and print the decoded result or revert
  decode  Decode call data, revert data or a log with an ABI, offline
  logs    Stream new heads or logs, or query logs over a block range
  tx      Show a transaction and its receipt, with input and logs decoded
  block   Show a block by number, tag or hash
  ens     Resolve an ENS name to an address, or an address to its verified primary name
  fork    Fork a chain with a local Anvil node and a temporary fork-<chain> environment, until Ctrl+C
  probe   Probe EVM RPC providers: method support, archive state, latency, subscriptions, rate limits and cross-provider consistency
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  rustman evm call requests/token/balance.rman.yaml --env mainnet
  rustman evm call --to 0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48 --abi erc20 --function balanceOf vitalik.eth --rpc {{rpc}}
  rustman evm decode --abi erc20 0xa9059cbb000...
  rustman evm logs --address 0xA0b8... --event "Transfer(address,address,uint256)" --max-events 5
  rustman evm tx 0x5c50... --env mainnet --json
  rustman evm block latest
  rustman evm ens vitalik.eth
  rustman evm fork --chain mainnet --block 20000000
  rustman evm probe https://rpc-a.example https://rpc-b.example
